Title: SECOND COAST
Author: Emily Nakamura
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. CAPE COD INN - PORCH - DAWN

Salt air. CLAIRE HART, 32, novelist, sips coffee. A taxi drops off JAMES MERCER, 34, carrying a battered LEATHER SATCHEL.
CLAIRE
You said you'd never come back east.
JAMES
I said a lot of things at twenty-four.

INT. INN LOBBY - MORNING

The innkeeper slides a key across the desk — adjacent rooms. James and Claire reach for it at the same time. Fingers brush. Both pull back.
CLAIRE
I'm here for the writers' retreat. Not a reunion tour.

EXT. BEACH - AFTERNOON

Claire walks the tide line. James catches up, shoes in hand. He pulls a folded PHOTO from the satchel — the two of them, younger, on this same beach.
JAMES
I kept it because we looked happy. I forgot we were.
CLAIRE
We were. Until we weren't.

INT. CLAIRE'S ROOM - NIGHT

Knock on the connecting door. Claire, the poet, sets down her pen and opens it a crack. James holds two paper cups of tea.
JAMES
You still take honey when you're stuck on a chapter.
CLAIRE
I'm stuck on a lot of things.

EXT. BEACH - SUNSET

They sit on the dunes, shoulders almost touching. The canvas satchel lies open between them — not the photo, but a manuscript draft with Claire's name on the dedication page.
CLAIRE
You wrote me into this before you wrote me out of your life.
JAMES
Maybe I came back to find out if there's a second draft.

FADE OUT.


THE END
